            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Bob's Red Mill protein powder healthy?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It is a clean, simple ingredient by label standards. The whey has two ingredients, and the almond and hemp powders have one each, with no added sugar, sweeteners, flavors or gums, per the labels at the time of writing. The trade-off is lower protein per scoop than sports powders and no third-party testing. Whether it is healthy for you depends on your overall diet and protein needs.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Bob's Red Mill whey protein contain lactose?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Yes, it contains some lactose. The bag is whey protein concentrate, which keeps more milk sugar than whey isolate, and the label lists 1 g of total sugar per 19 g serving. Bob's Red Mill does not publish a separate lactose figure. It is also a milk allergen. If lactose gives you trouble, a whey isolate or a plant powder such as the almond protein is a safer choice.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Bob's Red Mill hemp protein powder gluten free?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Not any more. The Bob's Red Mill product page states that the hemp protein powder is no longer produced gluten free, and it carries no gluten-free badge. Some older retailer listings still describe it as gluten free, so trust the current bag over the listing. Of the three current powders, only the almond protein powder shows a gluten-free badge on the brand's website.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Which Bob's Red Mill protein powder is best?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  For most people the whey is best: it has the highest protein density, about 74% by weight, and the lowest cost per 25 g of the three at about $1.61 at the Amazon price we saw. Buyers rate it 4.9 out of 5 on the brand's site. Choose the almond powder if you are vegan or need gluten free, and the hemp powder if fiber and iron are your priority.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are the common complaints about Bob's Red Mill protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
